          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %em uniqueness of identity proofs
            or
            %em UIP
            refers to a couple of different axioms and rules applicable to individual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            to turn them into
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+families"} type families
            to turn them into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/families+of+sets"} families of sets
            (and in particular,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universes"} universes
            to turn them into internal types of sets), as well as the type theory as a whole to turn it into an actual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set-level+type+theory"} set-level type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+universe"} univalent universe
          %p
            Heuristically, the axiom asserts that for each element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
