                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{UIP}_{A, B}: \prod_{a:A} \prod_{b:B(a)} \prod_{c:B(a)} \prod_{p:\mathrm{Id}_{B(a)}(b, c)} \prod_{q:\mathrm{Id}_{B(a)}(b, c)} \mathrm{Id}_{\mathrm{Id}_{B(a)}(b, c)}(p, q)
          %p
            This definition of uniqueness of identity proofs could be used in the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+sets"} family of sets
            %strong familial uniqueness of identity proofs
            to distinguish it from the uniqueness of identity proofs axiom above.
          %p
            Since every Tarski universe consists of a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            of encodings and a type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            representing the actual small types indexed by the type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            under all type formers, the familial uniqueness of identity proofs definition works for Tarski universes as well, and this could equivalently be called the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Tarski universe uniqueness of identity proofs
          %h3#as_a_rule_in_the_type_theory As a rule in the type theory
          %p
            Uniqueness of identity proofs could also be rewritten as a rule instead of an axiom, by making the hypotheses of the axioms into premises of the rule. This makes uniqueness of identity proofs applicable not only to universes, but to the entire type theory. In addition, one could use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
            in addition to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typal+equality"} typal equality
            = succeed "," do
              %strong judgmental uniqueness of identity proofs
            %strong typal uniqueness of identity proofs
          %p In this manner, uniqueness of identity proofs then becomes the rules:
          %ul
            %li Judgmental uniqueness of identity proofs
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
