                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h3#uniqueness_of_identity_proofs_and_univalence Uniqueness of identity proofs and univalence
          %p
            In this section we assume that the universe is a Tarski universe. Uniqueness of identity proofs is inconsistent with having a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+type+with+a+type+family"} univalent type with a type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, B)
            with at least one term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            where the dependent type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(a)
            is provably not a proposition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\prod_{p:B(a)}  \prod_{q:B(a)} \mathrm{Id}_{B(a)}(p, q)\right) \to \emptyset
          %p
            because by univalence,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is then provably not a set, which contradicts uniqueness of identity proofs. In particular, having a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+universe"} univalent universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U, T)
            in the type theory is inconsistent with uniqueness of identity proofs.
          %p
            The familial uniqueness of identity proofs axiom applied to Tarski universes implies that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U
            the type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A)
            is a set. This means the type reflection of the internal equivalences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A \simeq_U B)
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            then implies that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-groupoid"} h-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            which can be proven not to be an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/booleans+type"} booleans type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is provably not an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
          %p
            However, unlike the case for uniqueness of identity proofs, the familial uniqueness of identity proofs and the univalence axiom for universes are inconsistent with each other only if the Tarski universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            has objects which can be proven not to be an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V:U
            where the type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(V)
            has terms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:T(V)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_V(A)
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
            which is not an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/booleans+type"} booleans type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(V)
            can be proven to not be a set, causing uniqueness of identity proofs for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            to be inconsistent with the existence of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V:U
            and univalence.
